      "description": "## Problem\n\nWhen the sync worker restarts while a batch is half written, the next run crashes on a unique constraint and never recovers.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Start the worker with `SYNC_BATCH_SIZE=500`.\n2. Send `SIGTERM` after the first chunk is flushed.\n3. Start the worker again.\n\n### Expected\n\n- The worker resumes from the last committed chunk.\n- No duplicate rows are written.\n\n```rust\nfn resume(batch: &Batch) -> Result<Cursor> {\n    let committed = batch.last_committed_chunk()?;\n    Ok(Cursor::after(committed))\n}\n```\n\nSee the [runbook](https://docs.example.test/runbooks/sync-worker) for the current workaround.",
      "creator": {
        "id": "f149cdf3-5ed5-5c4a-b895-0af7f5a07d72",
        "name": "Chloe Tanaka",
        "displayName": "chloe",
        "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.example.test/chloe.png"
      },
